{
  "id": "automaintenance",
  "term": "automaintenance",
  "definition": "Automaintenance is a conditioned tendency to make a response toward a cue that predicts reward, such as pecking a lighted key after it has been paired with food. In negative automaintenance, this response can persist even though pecking causes the expected reward to be withheld.",
